// Native canonical-IPA data manifest for Min Dong / Eastern Min (cdo) — Fuzhou dialect (Fuzhounese), Sinitic,
// tonal, ~9M. Consumed by foochow.ts. Input orthography = Bàng-uâ-cê (BUC / Foochow Romanized), the phonemic
// missionary Latin script (cdo Wikipedia + historical press). The converter: [initial] + rime + tone diacritic → IPA.
// BUC missionary convention: plain ⟨p t k⟩ = ASPIRATED [pʰ tʰ kʰ], ⟨b d g⟩ = [p t k]; ⟨c⟩=[t͡s], ⟨ch⟩=[t͡sʰ], ⟨ng⟩=[ŋ].
// Maps DERIVED (reference-parity) from BUC↔IPA pairs in the kaikki Chinese dump (Wiktionary Module:cdo-pron output),
// cross-checked against the documented Foochow-Romanized tables. Phase 1 = segmental + citation tone; the 韻變 (rime
// alternation, a~ɑ/o~ɔ/e~ɛ) + tone sandhi + Han front-end are deferred/folded. See the investigation doc.
{
    "language": "cdo",
    "name": "Min Dong (Fuzhou / Eastern Min)",
    "script": "Latin (Bàng-uâ-cê) + Han",
    "initials": {
